      "message": "Not a blocker to submission, but trying to understand: \n\nI\u0027m only finding a tcpci rev 2 v.1.0 spec on usb.org. (is that good enough? I think so. https://www.usb.org/sites/default/files/documents/usb-port_controller_specification_rev2.0_v1.0_0.pdf)\n\nWhy is auto-discharge-disconnect related to the suzy-q? Shouldn\u0027t the DUT be the SNK in this case? \n    -do we get a disconnect in the PD negotiation process and so we force it back to 5V and that breaks things?\n",
